# Line endings are pinned here, not left to each checkout's core.autocrlf.
#
# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which would check every script out with CRLF, and
# bash then stops on the first line with `$'\r': command not found` (./setup, ./gradlew, the gates,
# the git hooks, and cloud/session_start.sh, which runs at the start of every Claude session). So
# everything text is LF in the working tree on every OS. The files cmd.exe reads are CRLF, stored that
# way and never converted (-text), so gradlew.bat stays byte-identical to Gradle's.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.bat  -text
*.cmd  -text

*.jar  binary
*.nbt  binary
*.png  binary
*.zip  binary
